  "id": "acetylsalicylic-acid",
  "term": "acetylsalicylic acid",
  "definition": "Acetylsalicylic acid (ASA, or aspirin) is a drug compound studied here for its effects on cancer progression and blood-platelet biology. In this mouse breast cancer model, long-term low-dose ASA changed platelet-related, inflammatory, and oxidative stress measures, but it did not reduce lung metastases and was associated with a less favorable disease pattern.",
